  "strategy": "Giada, Font of Hope makes every Angel after her enter with a +1/+1 counter for each Angel you already control, so the deck is a mono-white flock that gets bigger with every body. Bishop of Wings, Righteous Valkyrie and Lyra Dawnbringer turn the Angels into life, and Exemplar of Light and Youthful Valkyrie turn that life and those arrivals into more counters. Reya Dawnbringer and Emeria Shepherd bring the fallen back, and a deep removal suite - Swords to Plowshares, Austere Command, Day of Judgment - keeps the skies clear. It wins in the air, a few fliers at a time, and the plan against a wrath is to rebuild faster than the table can.",
  "signature": [
    {
      "card_id": "giada_font_of_hope",
      "why": "Every Angel after her lands with a counter for each Angel already there."
    },
    {
      "card_id": "lyra_dawnbringer",
      "why": "Lifelink and +1/+1 for every other Angel: each combat is lifegain."
    },
    {
      "card_id": "bishop_of_wings",
      "why": "Four life for each Angel that enters, a 1/1 Spirit flier for each one that dies."
    },
    {
      "card_id": "reya_dawnbringer",
      "why": "Returns a creature from the graveyard to the battlefield every upkeep."
    }
  ],
